    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d272">

                <pb facs="0551" n="455" xml:id="pg455"/>

                <head>No. 270.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Cadwalader to Mr. Nicholas
                            Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-08-01"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 1,
                        1874</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 689.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch of the 15th ultimo, No. 4,
                    inclosing, with extracts from the German press, a copy of your note of the 14th
                    ultimo to Prince Bismarck, congratulating him upon his escape from
                    assassination, has been received.</p>
                <p>Your action in congratulating the prince, as “communicated by telegraph, has
                    already been approved in No. 684, trom the Department.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN L. CADWALADER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                            Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
